  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-05-02T03:09:24.342Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Player movement has terrible latency, which is bad for game worlds. It would be great to have a world option to use predictive, low latency movement. A realtime-focused option would allow worlds where responsive player positioning matters to be more engaging and improve gameplay.\n\nExamples of worlds that would benefit:\n\n- Murder, Prison Escape, Among Us, Trash Compactor, Blackout, Magic Freeze Tag, MELA, Infected, Victory of Round, Spook Em Up, Ghost, VRC Volleyball, Probability Labs, GIGAS, Magic Arena\n\nThis wouldn't need to be in sync with player IK/audio. The option would focus purely on updating player positions as quickly as possible.",
